#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""<the same measurement question as in PROTOCOL-<name>.md, one sentence>

Usage:
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --show 3
        The config and three feature rows per split; no fit.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --probe
        Instrument check: twelve labelled items, reduced estimator at fit
        or the unchanged predictor at apply (its null on permuted labels),
        both lanes, into a throwaway file; prints the scores (not reported)
        and one row per lane as the run will keep them.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --calibrate-null
        Apply with the seeded permuted null: the unchanged predictor's
        predictions on the labelled items, fixed, scored against the
        registered rule's permutations of their gold; prints their spread
        and the permitted deviation the rule gives — what each run computes
        for itself. A preview: No run, nothing written, and the predictions
        are never scored against their true gold.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py
        The full run, recorded by runlog (at high repeat cost: `runlog start
        <area> -- …`, after the freeze and the preflight audit).
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --eval-only
        Re-evaluate the kept rows; no fit.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --repeat-of RUN_ID
        The kept run RUN_ID drawn again with a seed labkit derives from it
        and the draw number (`answering_run.repeat_seed`), everything else
        unchanged: a run of its own (repeat_of) into <out>_draw<N>.jsonl —
        the spread over seeds, never the answer. `02_analyze.py --draws`
        shows it.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --seed 7
        A measurement with another seed: a full run like the one above,
        which answers the protocol when it is the newest — the spread is
        `--repeat-of`, not this.

The protocol's kind chooses the instrument. At `fit`, `make_estimator()`
creates an estimator with fit(X, y) and predict(X): the registered lane
fits true labels, the null lane fits labels permuted inside each fitting
fold, and the test lane fits every labelled item before predicting the
unlabelled split. Every scored prediction is out of fold.
At `apply`, `make_estimator()` loads the unchanged predictor with
predict(X); it is never fitted and never sees gold. Its null lane scores
the same predictions against the gold labels permuted with the seed —
each null row names whose label it carries (`gold_of`) —, so the noise
floor needs no second instrument. What those predictions reach against
randomly assigned labels on average is exact, no draw
(`permutation_expectation()`): [criterion-1]'s bar is it plus `margin`, and [quality-check-2]
holds the one permuted draw — the anchor in the same run — within the
permitted deviation of it (the null-check interval, inclusive). The
protocol registers the rule, not the value (LAB-035 Thresholds belong to
the run, not to the measure): `null_band_quantile` over `null_permutations`
permutations of the gold, seeded by `null_band_seed` — a calibration seed
apart from the run's seed. Every evaluation computes the permitted
deviation from the run's own registered predictions and gold
(`run_null_band`, `deviation_by_rule`), keeps it as `quality_check_2_null_band`
and compares with it; the same inputs give the same value, whatever the
run's seed or the rows' order. Predictions that score alike under every
permutation (one answer for every item) get 0, an exact null check;
none at all, or none in the gold's labels, are refused. Registering
`null_band` there is refused. `--calibrate-null` previews it. A
protocol that registers a
fixed null order (`NULL_ORDER`: a permutation file the organizer drew once)
gets that order in the seed's place: it is one fixed control, so its score
plus `margin` is the bar, and [quality-check-2]'s permitted deviation, a
reasoned `null_band`, applies only where the protocol registers one (the
order's validity is checked when it is read). A
protocol that registers a fixed null predictor
returns it from `make_null_predictor()` instead; its score plus `margin`
is the bar, and [quality-check-2] holds it within a registered `null_band` of `chance_of()`. At fit
the null lane refits on permuted labels `null_refits` times per fold (the
fit plan by repeat cost, `FIT_PLAN`), each draw seeded from the run's seed, its fold and its number: [criterion-1]'s bar is the
mean of their scores plus `margin`, [quality-check-2] holds that mean within
`null_band` of `chance_of()`, and the draws' scores (`quality_check_2_draw_scores`)
show how far one strays — one refit's draw decided a fit's verdict
(fourth SAB-like draw: the kept score = `criterion_1_threshold`). A registered constant changed after the first measurement is
refused (report-check). All lanes are
recorded in the same run (LAB-034 Null condition in the same run).
Unlabelled predictions are never scored.

Measurement contract:
  - Every labelled item is predicted once per scored lane in the same run;
    `fit` uses out-of-fold fitting, `apply` uses unchanged predictors.
  - The score (`SCORE`: accuracy · r2 · auc · spearman) is over EVERY
    labelled item of the lane: an item without a prediction scores as wrong
    (accuracy), as the mean (r2) or ranks below every real prediction (auc,
    spearman), and is counted on its own as `quality_check_1_empty`.
  - The registered lane's score is the kept number: computed once, stored
    under the key the protocol head's `[kept]` names (`KEPT_KEY`; key and
    unit set there, never here), on every evaluation — also when a quality
    check fails, where it stays visible and no criterion judges it.
  - [criterion-1], offered commented out — optional while the protocol is
    exploratory, owed when it is confirmatory: two steps turn it on, both
    owed, (1) its table in the protocol's block uncommented and its id
    named in the Inference criterion field, (2) the block between the
    `criterion-1` markers in evaluate_rows below uncommented. Without it
    the kept score is reported without a success verdict. It passes when
    the kept score is at least its
    bar, registered in one of two forms (LAB-035 Thresholds belong to the
    run, not to the measure): `at_least`, a bar the task states, is the
    bar as written, whatever the null lane scores; `margin` is a lead over
    the null value — at apply with the permuted null its exact expectation
    (`permutation_expectation`), at fit the mean of the `null_refits`
    permuted-label refits, with a fixed null predictor its score. A task's
    absolute bar written as a margin moves with the predictions: accuracy's
    expectation is theirs, a fit's refits are random.
  - [quality-check-1] checks the yield (at most `max_empty` labelled items without a
    prediction); [quality-check-2] that the null lane scores within the permitted
    deviation of its target — computed per run at apply with the seeded
    permuted null, a registered `null_band` otherwise — the permutation
    expectation at apply, chance otherwise
    (`chance_of`, derived, not guessed). If either fails, [criterion-1] has no
    verdict (None).
  - [criterion-2], offered commented out, no duty: the registered lane's
    score strictly exceeds the comparison threshold, the permutation
    expectation plus the run's permitted deviation — the threshold derived
    from randomly permuted labels; nothing about size. Two steps turn it on, both
    owed: (1) uncomment its table in the protocol's block and name the id
    in the Inference criterion field; (2) uncomment the block between the
    `criterion-2` markers in evaluate_rows below. Step 1 alone: code-check
    blocks, no script reports the key; step 2 alone: code-check warns of an
    unregistered key and intent-check blocks. Apply with the permuted null
    and the registered calibration rule only; elsewhere the permitted deviation is no permutation
    quantile, and null_check refuses before the run opens (evaluate_rows
    by the rows' shape). No verdict when a quality check fails. What the
    comparison licenses beyond that, and what it does not:
    docs/notes/2026-11-14-apply-chance-comparison.md.
  - A withheld label is no label: the prepare step writes `gold: null` for
    the unlabelled split (a test file storing 0 or -999 is a placeholder),
    and a lane carrying an item without gold is never scored — a criterion
    on zero gold once "passed" (haiku t3, labkit-paper area 09, 2026-10-16).
  - `evaluate_rows()` is the only implementation of these formulas;
    `02_analyze.py` and the test import it, never copy it.
  - The protocol owns the registered thresholds; `MeasureConfig` holds them
    for one execution; config.json records that object whole.
  - A seed is a source of randomness, so the protocol's randomness and
    noise-ceiling fields are owed. Measure the spread on the probe or on
    the null lane; the registered lane on all items before the freeze makes
    the freeze empty (Sonnet v3 t3 and t5, 2026-10-16).

A task that names its output file (`pred_results/<name>.csv`) is answered
by that file: DELIVERABLES names it, deliverable_rows() gives its rows from
the kept rows and the metrics, and the full run writes and registers it
(`write_deliverables`; a repeat's draw writes none) — its sha256 lands in
the run's outputs.json, and `finalize` holds the file in the tree to it.
Never write it by hand.

Why (house rules, one per line so a reference is never cut):
  LAB-034 Null condition in the same run
  LAB-035 Thresholds belong to the run
  LAB-041 Generate numbers, don't retype them
  LAB-004 Identifiers make the intent addressable
  LAB-016 Resolution check before freezing
  LAB-023 No silent loss
Stamped by `labkit-init exp <name>` (no --model); fill the TODOs, keep the structure.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
